(footprint "LuckFox_Pico_Mini" (version 20211014) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "B.Cu")
  (tedit 63DAF38E)
  (descr "Cutout + edge-castellation mount for LuckFox Pico Mini, MIRRORED (component side, incl. camera FPC connector, faces AWAY from the shield -- accessible from outside once assembled) -- module nests underneath the shield through this slot. U-shaped opening: enclosed on left/right/top, OPEN on the bottom edge (the USB-C end, post-mirror) so the module's USB-C connector can extend past the shield's own board edge. The open side only works if this footprint is positioned so that opening actually reaches your board's real outer edge -- it is not automatically merged with your board outline. 22 castellated edge pads lap-solder directly to the pads here -- no header/socket. Cutout sized to LuckFox's 21.00x28.14mm outline plus 0.15mm clearance per side; pads centered on LuckFox's nominal edge line (2.54mm pitch, 17.78mm row spacing, per LuckFox's official mechanical drawing) so they straddle the routed slot edge. Pin-row order is reversed vs the unmirrored version: real pin 11/12 (camera-connector end) are now at the top (y=1.37), real pin 1/22 (USB-C end) now at the bottom (y=26.77). Confirm the 0.15mm clearance and pad size against your fab house's minimum slot/annular tolerances before ordering.")
